# API Synchronization Rule

## When this applies
Any edit to API communications between Flutter and Python, including:
- Endpoint paths, query params, or JSON keys
- Request/response payload shapes or field defaults
- Image array dimensionality/encoding from `/images`
- Filters/variables handling or histogram length in `/distributions`
- Manipulated dimension naming/aliasing that affects mapping

## Required actions
1) Update `docs/API_COMMUNICATION.md` with the exact contract and examples.
2) Update the opposite side to match in the same change:
   - If Flutter changed, update Flask handlers in `app.py` (and `parse_config`) and related logic in `gan_backend.py`.
   - If Python changed, update Flutter datasources and entities under `lib/features/face_generation/`.
3) Build and stage:
   - Run `flutter build web --release`
   - `git add build/web`

## Paths to review
- Frontend: `lib/features/face_generation/data/datasources/*`, `lib/features/face_generation/domain/entities/*`
- Backend: `app.py` (routes `/images`, `/distributions`), `gan_backend.py`

## Done checklist
- [ ] Doc updated (`docs/API_COMMUNICATION.md`)
- [ ] Other side updated
- [ ] Web build succeeded and `build/web` staged

